  "question": {
    "text": "A physical quantity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> is found to depend on quantities <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>c</mi></math> by the relation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math>. The percentage error in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>b</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>%</mo><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>4</mn><mo>%</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>%</mo></math> respectively. Then, the percentage error in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> is:",
